# Plant Pact environment variables.
#
# Local development needs NONE of these: when DATABASE_URL is unset outside
# production the app runs on an embedded PGlite database stored in ./.pglite.
#
# Production (Vercel) REQUIRES DATABASE_URL. Without it the production build
# refuses to open the repository rather than silently falling back to a
# non-durable store. Plant Pact intentionally has no third-party API keys:
# Open-Meteo and the GBIF Backbone Taxonomy are public, keyless endpoints.

# Hosted Postgres connection string (Neon via the Vercel Marketplace, or any
# other provider). Supplied automatically by the Vercel Neon integration.
# DATABASE_URL=postgresql://user:password@host/dbname?sslmode=require

# Optional: schema namespace so the app can share one database instance with
# other projects. Defaults to the public schema.
# DATABASE_SCHEMA=plant_pact

# Optional: absolute canonical origin used for metadata, sitemap and the MCP
# manifest. Defaults to the VERCEL_URL/VERCEL_PROJECT_PRODUCTION_URL that
# Vercel injects, and falls back to http://localhost:3000 locally.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=https://plant-pact.vercel.app

# Optional: force the sealed offline weather sample without any network access.
# Used by the deterministic unit tests and by offline local smoke runs.
# PLANT_PACT_OFFLINE=1

# Optional, LOCAL SMOKE TESTS ONLY. Allows the production build to run against
# the embedded PGlite store so `npm run smoke` can exercise the real production
# bundle without a database. Data is NOT durable. Never set this in a real
# deployment: a production instance without DATABASE_URL must fail to boot
# rather than accept writes into volatile storage.
# PLANT_PACT_ALLOW_EMBEDDED=1

# Optional: set to "1" to skip the HTTP-only session cookie when the app is
# behind a trusted proxy that terminates TLS. Not required on Vercel.
# TRUST_PROXY_COOKIES=1